From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] feat(libc): stream read-only app0 archive stdio

Preserve the guest FILE prefix and loose-file behavior while routing archive
streams through the existing shared archive descriptor cursor. Use native
FILE objects only for descriptor lifetime and locking, never archive bytes.

Implement archive opening, reads, character and status operations, positions,
pushback, flushing, descriptor sharing and reopening. Stream narrow scanf
fields incrementally and reject unsupported operations explicitly. Synchronize
backend transitions after descriptor replacement and preserve reopening kinds.

Exercise root param.sfx, binary odx fallback, compressed-block reads, damaged
input, partial elements, guest layout, scanning, shared kernel positions,
read-only refusals, descriptor cleanup and concurrent backend transitions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
